'''''Tolpis barbata''''' is a species of flowering plant in the family [[Asteraceae]] known by the common name '''European umbrella milkwort'''.<ref>{{PLANTS|id=TOBA|taxon=Tolpis barbata|accessdate=11 December 2015}}</ref> It is native to southern Europe, including the [[Mediterranean Basin|Mediterranean]], namely in Portugal, Spain, Morocco, Algeria, Tunisia and the British territory of Gibraltar<ref>{{cite web |title=World Plants: Complete Plant List |url=http://www.worldplants.de/?deeplink=Tolpis-barbata |website=www.worldplants.de |access-date=21 November 2022}}</ref><ref>{{cite web |title=Tolpis barbata (L.) Gaertn. {{!}} Plants of the World Online {{!}} Kew Science |url=https://powo.science.kew.org/taxon/urn:lsid:ipni.org:names:255787-1 |website=Plants of the World Online |access-date=21 November 2022 |language=en}}</ref> and it is known in many other places as an [[introduced species]] and a common [[weed]], such as in [[California]]<ref>[http://ucjeps.berkeley.edu/cgi-bin/get_JM_treatment.pl?609,1926,1927 Jepson Manual Treatment]</ref> and [[New South Wales]].<ref>[http://plantnet.rbgsyd.nsw.gov.au/cgi-bin/NSWfl.pl?page=nswfl&lvl=sp&name=Tolpis~barbata New South Wales Flora]</ref>

